(7439083, 1176004, 113411, '<td valign="top">Great portrait Jeff. It seems that so many people want to know your technique and since The Godfather sent it to me, I thought I would share it.<br/>//wegraphics.net/blog/tutorials/photoshop-quick-tip-create-a-dragan-style-portrait-effect-in-5-steps/</td>', 'Great portrait Jeff. It seems that so many people want to know your technique and since The Godfather sent it to me, I thought I would share it.//wegraphics.net/blog/tutorials/photoshop-quick-tip-create-a-dragan-style-portrait-effect-in-5-steps/', '2016-02-23 17:13:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439114, 1176004, 89723, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MeMex2:</b></div><hr/><i> Great portrait Jeff. It seems that so many people want to know your technique and since The Godfather sent it to me, I thought I would share it.<br/>//wegraphics.net/blog/tutorials/photoshop-quick-tip-create-a-dragan-style-portrait-effect-in-5-steps/ </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m certainly familiar with "Dragan" style and have influences from it. I don''t follow any of those steps. I used "high pass" quite a bit in the past, but now I''ve found some other techniques that appeal to me. That''s the wonderful thing about this art form. So many different ways to get to a certain outcome.  <br/> <br/>Here is the original:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1176384" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1176384.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1176384.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1176384.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by MeMex2: Great portrait Jeff. It seems that so many people want to know your technique and since The Godfather sent it to me, I thought I would share it.//wegraphics.net/blog/tutorials/photoshop-quick-tip-create-a-dragan-style-portrait-effect-in-5-steps/   I''m certainly familiar with "Dragan" style and have influences from it. I don''t follow any of those steps. I used "high pass" quite a bit in the past, but now I''ve found some other techniques that appeal to me. That''s the wonderful thing about this art form. So many different ways to get to a certain outcome.   Here is the original:   ', '2016-02-23 18:02:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439130, 1175435, 101707, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PaulFrocchi:</b></div><hr/><i> this has such a great feel to it.  Is that an American flag in the subtly peeking out? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Paul. Yes it is the American flag. I had intended on naming this ''Fortress America" but thought i''d keep it more neutral.</td>', 'Originally posted by PaulFrocchi: this has such a great feel to it.  Is that an American flag in the subtly peeking out?   Thanks Paul. Yes it is the American flag. I had intended on naming this ''Fortress America" but thought i''d keep it more neutral.', '2016-02-23 19:12:32.000000', NULL, 0),
